That is not what this video is about.
What I want to talk about is some of the

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.810
risks and concerns that have been
uncovered in the literature that are

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:08.459
specific and unique to this population
so you can embark on your health and

00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:13.500
fitness journey in the healthiest way
possible. First of all, let's talk

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.240
about the physical dangers and risks
starting with potential nutrition

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.570
deficiencies. One of the major concerns
with bodybuilding and fitness

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:26.490
competition prep is the risk for
micronutrient deficiencies and this is

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:30.090
because of the tendencies for some
bodybuilders to have to severely

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:35.310
restrict certain foods in their diet and
only include a small range of repeated

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:40.920
"safe" foods on their plan. Some studies on
dieting competitors observe deficiencies

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:46.320
in micronutrients like vitamin D, calcium,
zinc, magnesium, and iron. Having said that,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.730
a lot of this evidence is from the early
days of bodybuilding so it's very

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.630
possible that these micronutrient
deficiencies were maybe more common in

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:58.080
those days due to very premature
understanding of bodybuilding nutrition

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:04.260
and drastic elimination diets. We've
definitely come a long way having said

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:08.190
that, in a lot of cases, especially for
women, it may be useful to take a

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:12.180
multivitamin if you are severely
restricting calories or certain types of

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:17.070
food in preparation for competition.
There is also the common risk of fluid

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:21.420
imbalances. Now in the final days and
hours before a fitness competition, also

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.130
known as "peak week", many bodybuilders
will attempt to manipulate their fluid

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:30.540
and electrolyte levels to improve their
muscularity and to get them that kind of

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:36.500
ripped appearance. Now in order to define
their muscularity during that final week

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.910
bodybuilders will kind of dramatically
increase their water intake, sometimes to

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:47.310
as much as 10 litres per day, while also
taking diuretics. Then the day before the

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.420
competition bodybuilders may be
instructed to dramatically cut their

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:57.120
water intake in order to dehydrate their
body sometimes getting no water for 24

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.299
hours before showtime
while continuing on their diuretic

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:03.570
supplements. Now I know we've been
conditioned to believe that more water

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:08.610
is better, but drinking 10 litres of
water a day and then flushing that out

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:13.709
with diuretics can easily cause water
intoxication, hyponatremia, and

00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:17.100
hypokalemia which taken together may be
fatal.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:22.490
Other side effects can include irregular
heartbeat, fatigue, seizures, GI distress,

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.040
muscle cramping and weakness, headaches,
and

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:31.890
more. Playing with water might even make
you look "too flat" depending on how and

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:36.960
when it's done. So you could actually put
yourself at risk and not even get the

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.730
desired look for competition. Now let's
talk about some supplement concerns.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:46.440
While the supplement industry's market
is worth as much as 37 billion dollars a

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:51.180
year, most researchers and health care
professionals caution their use because

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:55.200
there really isn't clear evidence that
they work and are beneficial to our

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.030
health. On top of that, because
supplements are not necessarily so well

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:05.310
regulated there are a ton of illegal
substances that make their way onto

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:10.440
store shelves and honestly they have
killed people. According to a 2016 study,

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.600
it's estimated that around 23,000
emergency room visits a year are linked

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.770
to supplements. Because of the lack of
regulation, consumers don't really know

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:24.330
all of the ingredients in supplements
and dosages could even vary from pill to

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:29.940
pill. That is really scary stuff and we
need greater regulation if it's causing

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:34.230
people to die. There's also potential
side effects of some common supplements

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:38.820
used for fitness competition. From
anxiety, insomnia, kidney and liver damage,

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:44.580
infertility, and even death. You really
have to trust your coach to prescribe

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:49.500
these cocktails of supplements and drugs
in appropriate doses for you. I don't

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:54.600
know about you, but that feels like it
takes a lot of trust. Now let's talk

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.740
about some of the psychological risks
including body dissatisfaction and

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.160
disordered eating.
in one study, one-third of a group of

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:07.200
bodybuilders reported anxiety, short
tempers, or anger during competition prep.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:13.110
Furthermore, 81.5% of them in the group
reported a preoccupation with food which

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:16.860
is a precursor of course to disordered
eating. This is especially a concern

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:21.180
among female fitness competitors as one
study found that among female

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:28.320
competitive bodybuilders about 42% used
to be anorexic, 67% were terrified of

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:33.540
becoming fat, and 50% experienced
uncontrollable urges to eat. Furthermore,

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.870
research gathered from the National
Eating Disorders website found that

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:42.339
among female high school athletes
41.5% reported disordered eating, and

00:06:42.339 --> 00:06:46.539
disordered eating affected 62% of female
athletes in aesthetic weight class

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:51.039
sports. I'll also just never forget a
story that my personal trainer told me

00:06:51.039 --> 00:06:54.849
about the competition floor.
He said that young female competitors

00:06:54.849 --> 00:07:00.309
all bring these suitcases filled with
cookies, candies, cupcakes, doughnuts, you

00:07:00.309 --> 00:07:04.149
know all the things that they haven't
allowed themselves to eat while doing

00:07:04.149 --> 00:07:08.589
their prep diet. Then the moment that
they get off stage, they tend to go crazy

00:07:08.589 --> 00:07:12.819
and literally eat until they make
themselves sick. So while you may look at

00:07:12.819 --> 00:07:17.110
a fitness competitor and assume that
they are the picture of perfect health,

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:21.459
it's very possible that some of these
behaviors may tell a very different

00:07:21.459 --> 00:07:26.499
story. This is just another perfect
example of how one's physical body is

00:07:26.499 --> 00:07:31.089
not necessarily a great depiction of
their actual health. You really cannot

00:07:31.089 --> 00:07:35.499
judge a book by its cover.
Now let's talk about my bread and butter,

00:07:35.499 --> 00:07:39.549
fertility. Anytime that you're severely
restricting calories or increasing

00:07:39.549 --> 00:07:43.539
activities, you put a woman at risk for
hormonal imbalance which may in turn

00:07:43.539 --> 00:07:48.819
impact fertility and overall health.
In one study, 25% of female bodybuilding

00:07:48.819 --> 00:07:52.869
competitors reported abnormal menstrual
cycles, while another study reported that

00:07:52.869 --> 00:07:56.079
women complained of menstrual
irregularity within the first month of

00:07:56.079 --> 00:08:00.159
competition prep. The researchers found
that caloric restriction led to a

00:08:00.159 --> 00:08:05.009
decline in fat and body mass which
resulted in the absent menstrual cycle.

00:08:05.009 --> 00:08:10.059
Restrictive diets, excessive exercise, low
body weight, and nutritional deficiencies

00:08:10.059 --> 00:08:15.819
from bodybuilding can lead to what we
call the "female athlete triad", which is a

00:08:15.819 --> 00:08:21.129
condition defined by a) low energy
available with or without disordered

00:08:21.129 --> 00:08:27.849
eating, b) menstrual dysfunction, and c)
low bone density. Research has also found

00:08:27.849 --> 00:08:31.929
that both resistance training and energy
restriction are associated with

00:08:31.929 --> 00:08:36.519
alterations in key reproductive hormones,
ultimately resulting in estrogen

00:08:36.519 --> 00:08:41.199
deficiency. Not only does this have an
impact on fertility, but a lack of

00:08:41.199 --> 00:08:46.180
estrogen can also cause a disruption in
bone remodeling which can increase the

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:50.590
risk of fractures and ultimately
osteoporosis.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.750
Finally, let's chat about the big elephant in the
room weight and metabolic declines.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:00.640
One of the main criticisms of rapid weight
loss or low calorie diets is that it may

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:05.230
slow down a person's metabolic rate. This
in turn makes it very difficult and

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:10.450
potentially even virtually impossible to
keep the weight off once a person stops

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:16.150
dieting and resumes to normal eating.
Even if their "normal eating" is still

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:20.860
very balanced and healthy. This combined
with the psychological drive to binge

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:26.890
eat all of the "forbidden foods" after a
show makes it very easy to see how a lot

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:31.450
of female fitness competitors kind of
bounce up to an even higher weight post

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:35.920
show than they were before they began.
Not surprisingly, there are a lot of

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:40.690
hormonal adaptations to blame for these
shifts. One, studies have found that a

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:45.190
low-calorie diet may decrease thyroid
hormone levels which can decrease a

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:49.690
person's overall metabolic rate. Two,
leptin which is our fullness hormone

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:55.060
lives in body fats so when we lower our
body fat levels leptin levels also

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:59.110
decline. Studies have shown that a low
calorie diet with an effort to promote

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:04.000
fat loss may decrease leptin levels
resulting in competitors feeling

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:10.240
basically constantly hungry and
prompting them to overeat. Three, ghrelin

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:14.710
which is our hunger hormone increases in
the body when we fast so researchers

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.760
have found that a low calorie diet can
increase ghrelin stimulating

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:23.500
participants to eat more. Four, researchers
also found that a low calorie diet

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.790
decreases our natural testosterone
levels and since testosterone plays an

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:31.630
important role in increasing muscle
protein synthesis and muscle mass it

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:37.600
could negatively impact metabolically
active muscle mass. And five, research has found

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:42.370
that a low calorie diet may increase
cortisol which has been shown to increase

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:47.230
protein breakdown and healthy subjects
again impacting metabolically active

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:53.020
tissue. Bottom line, before I leave you
let's get one thing straight. I am by no

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:56.980
means trying to say that you shouldn't
become a female fitness competitor or

00:10:56.980 --> 00:11:02.020
bodybuilder if that is what brings you
joy. My job as a dietitian is to try to

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:05.610
understand this athletic
trend, to dive into the culture, and

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:09.570
explore the possible concerns with
following this type of lifestyle, and of

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:13.680
course to give you the tools that you
need to do it in the safest way possible.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:18.480
My recommendation? Seek out an
experienced sports dietitian who can

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:22.980
really help guide you through this
process in the safest way possible and

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:27.420
do a real deep dive to ensure that
you're psychologically ready for what it

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:31.950
entails. Personally, I know that this
would take me to some dangerously dark

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:36.150
places so it would never be a healthy
sport for me.

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:39.900
I am simply presenting the literature
and what it has uncovered in terms of

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:44.970
concerns and risks and that way you can
hopefully make the most informed choices

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:50.820
for yourself. On that note, please keep
